questions.explanation:
Step 1: Evaluate Statement I. In 1913, the English physicist Henry Moseley observed the characteristic X-ray spectra of various elements by bombarding them with high-energy cathode rays. Thus, Statement I is correct.
Step 2: Evaluate Statement II. Moseley observed that a plot of $\sqrt{
u}$ against atomic number ($Z$) yielded a straight line, satisfying the equation $\sqrt{
u} = a(Z - b)$, whereas the plot of $\sqrt{
u}$ against atomic mass ($A$) did not yield a straight line. This showed that atomic number, not atomic weight, is the fundamental property of an element. Thus, Statement II is incorrect.
Conclusion: Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.
